pavel: Heads-up — onboarding sampleapp throwing a weird embedding/rerank parity issue across Node + Python that looks subtly different from the usual nested-array problem. Thought I'd surface here before opening a ticket.

nina: what are you seeing?

pavel: Repro is small. When batching a single short input, Node helper returns a vector of length 1535 (one token missing) inside an outer array while Python returns the full 1536-length vector. Downstream distance math fails with dim mismatch. Also rerank responses from one hosted variant returned `score_value` (not `score` or `ranking_score`). To make things worse, our Node auth retry resend drops the x-rw-idempotency header resulting in duplicate writes for some workflows. Logs & snippets: 

```
# Node helper use (sampleapp v1.2.0)
const batch = batchingHelper([{text: 'search me'}]);
// batch -> [ [0.12, 0.05, ..., <1535 numbers> ] ]

// API accepted it but retriever errors: "vector dim mismatch: expected 1536, got 1535"

# Python
b = batching.make(['search me'])
# b -> [0.12, 0.05, ..., <1536 numbers> ]

// Rerank hosted response observed last night:
{ "results": [{ "id": "doc-123", "score_value": 0.77 }] }
// our sdk mapping only checks for `score` and `ranking_score` right now.

// Auth retry trace:
[auth] 401 -> refresh token -> resend request without x-rw-idempotency-token -> server processed twice

```

carlos: That's odd — 1-off vector length sounds like a flattening/trim bug in the Node helper's final stage. Can you dump the raw payload before any local packing and the exact header set?

pavel: Pasted headers & raw payload lines (sensitive bits redacted):

```
POST /v1/embeddings
Headers: Authorization: Bearer <redacted>, x-rw-client-id: abc-123, x-rw-idempotency-token: client-xyz
Body: { "input": ["search me"], "model": "open-embed-1536" }

Node helper pre-serialize vector sample (first 8 values): [0.12,0.05,0.001,...,0.34] length: 1536
Node helper post-serialize payload shows truncated tail on buffer write (length 1535)
```

riley: I can take the Node helper. My suspicion: a Buffer.slice or typed-array copy with an off-by-one when wrapping into an outer array for single items. I'll add unit tests that assert length==D for D in fixtures.

nina: For the rerank `score_value` — we've seen a model bump that renamed the field in a canary. SDK should normalize accepted keys: `score`, `ranking_score`, `score_value`, `confidence` (in that priority). Can we add a small compatibility layer in sampleapp so new users don't get tripped?

pavel: I've added a short client-side shim in the sampleapp template that normalizes both embedding shape and rerank keys. Snippet: 

```js
// embeddings shape normalization
let vecs = resp.data;
if (!Array.isArray(vecs[0])) vecs = [vecs];
// ensure each vector has expected length D
vecs = vecs.map(v => v.length === D ? v : padOrFail(v, D));
// rerank score normalizer
const mapped = res.results.map(r => ({ id: r.id, score: r.score ?? r.ranking_score ?? r.score_value ?? r.confidence }));
```

carlos: Good short-term. Longer-term: Node helper should guarantee not to mutate numeric buffers and to preserve full length. Also auth middleware must preserve idempotency token across retries. I'll open a PR for the helper and tag riley.

riley: I'll add unit tests for single-item and multi-item batches and assert no truncation. Also adding a fuzz test using fixed-seed random vectors to catch edge-case buffer issues.

harmony-bot: Created ticket DEVEX-3199: "sampleapp: Node embedding helper truncates vectors for n=1 + rerank key variance + auth retry idempotency header preservation". Linked PRs requested: prs/7350 (node-buffer-fix), prs/7351 (sdk-rerank-normalize), prs/7352 (auth-retry-preserve-idempotency). Request: include e2e parity test in sampleapp comparing Node & Py outputs on a fixed fixture.

docs: I'll draft a short onboarding note mentioning that rerank field names may vary by model and that the sampleapp includes normalization shims until SDK patches land. I'll also add a troubleshooting checklist: 1) check vector length equals D, 2) check rerank key mapping, 3) verify x-rw-idempotency-token is set.

pavel: Thanks all. I'll link the logs & the sampleapp branch to DEVEX-3199. Once node PR lands, we can remove the temporary padOrFail and rely on SDK contract. Appreciate the quick turn on this. :rocket:
